## Does tests/docs/test_onboarding_deck.py need an update?

No change. The test checks two things: every command and flag shown in `<code>` and in SVG `<text>`, `<title>` and `<desc>` exists in the guide (test:69-87), and the footer keeps the "Built from HOW-WE-WORK.md at commit <sha>" shape (test:23, :90-91). Both still pass on the updated deck (`./artifacts/t6-tests.log`). It cannot tell whether a route or a prose sentence matches the guide (a stale `/roadmap` default would pass because `/roadmap` exists in the guide); this grep log, the per-task reviews and the Task 7 accuracy review cover that. Adding prose-level assertions would pin today's wording and break on every guide edit, so it is left to the review steps rather than the test.
